{
  "title": "Catalog: pick turkey and pork ground-meat blends from a stated percentage (\"93/7 ground turkey\")",
  "description": "prepared_form (ramekin-core/src/catalog/mod.rs) swaps in a ground-meat blend only when the resolved entry id contains beef's wording \"N% lean meat / M% fat\". \
Turkey and pork default to blendless entries (\"turkey, ground, raw\", \"pork, ground, raw\"), and USDA spells their blends differently: \"turkey, ground, 93% lean, 7% fat, raw\" and \"pork, ground, 84% lean / 16% fat, raw\". \
As a result, a stated percentage doesn't pick these blends in any position: in the note (\"ground turkey\" / \"93% lean\"), after the noun (\"ground turkey, 93% lean\"), or leading the item (\"93/7 ground turkey\", from the onceuponachef--recipes-turkey-spinach-cheese- fixture). \
Lines that don't match a curated alias stay unresolved, or resolve to the generic food in the note case. \
Fix: for a ground turkey/pork entry, try the species' USDA blend names (\"<meat>, ground, L% lean, F% fat, raw\", \"<meat>, ground, L% lean / F% fat, raw\") and take one only when it exists exactly, as the beef rule does. \
Raised in review of the leading-blend PR (#789). \
Expect small data/ diffs from make pipeline (nutrition coverage). \
Server-side catalog only, so no web or iOS changes. \
Bump catalog RULE_VERSION.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
